WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:24.740
CLAY: I am delighted
to welcome you

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.070
and to welcome Dr.
John Hume, our guest,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.530
for the third Ford/MIT
Nobel Laureate Lecture.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.540
The Nobel Prize
recognizes contributions

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.900
of uncommon excellence and
impact in a variety of fields.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.340
Dr. Hume's Peace Prize in 1998
is in that great tradition.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.400
I'm also delighted to
acknowledge the Ford Motor

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.760
Company for its support of
this lecture series, that

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.610
aims to bring the very best
thinking on great issues

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.740
to the MIT community.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.950
We are also grateful for the
cooperation of the MIT Lecture

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.440
Series Committee,
the Graduate Student

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.660
Council, and the
Undergraduate Association.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.120
A couple of
housekeeping matters.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.870
After the lecture, Dr.
Hume will accept questions

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.460
from the audience.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.710
And following the program,
we invite the audience

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:22.170
to a reception in the lobby
of the Student Center.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.180
Finally, a future note.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.400
On Tuesday, February 19, 2002,
the fourth Nobel Laureate

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.360
Lecture will be given by Dr.
David Baltimore, President

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.150
of the California
Institute of Technology,

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.235
and winner of the
Nobel Prize in biology.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.520
In 1998, the Nobel Committee
recognized Dr. John Hume

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.700
and David Trimble for
their contributions

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.980
to peace in Northern Ireland.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.460
For more than 30 years,
violence and unrest

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:58.430
based on religious, political,
and social unrest and bias

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.310
in Northern Ireland cost
more than 3,500 lives,

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.150
and caused untold
horror and pain.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:09.840
The presence of violence
stunted economic growth,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.790
that fed even more violence.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.830
Throughout this.
period, John Hume

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.040
was the most articulate
voice in Northern Ireland's

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.500
political leadership
and the struggle

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.300
to achieve a just peace.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.720
Dr. Hume started on
the path toward peace

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.270
as a leader of the
nonviolent civil rights

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.540
movement in the late 1960s.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.600
He went on to establish a
record of community leadership.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.590
He served as a special adviser
to the European Community

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.790
Commissioner and
various other groups.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.590
Dr. Hume is presently a member
of the British and European

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.330
Parliaments.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.600
Dr. Hume played two important
other critical roles.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.290
He helped to create institutions
in Europe and in Ireland

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:59.550
that respected diversity, such
as the Council of Ministers,

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.420
the European Commission,
and the European Parliament.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.300
Drawing on the European
strength, the solidarity

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.600
with American and European
peace collaborators,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.650
he was able to bring out
the best among all parties

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.440
to create a lasting peace.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.010
Dr. Hume also recognized
the powerful connection

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.770
between economic
development and peace,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.380
and is now a champion
for the nation

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.800
building that will ultimately
keep conflict under control.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.590
It is fitting, in this
current conflict and outrage

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.350
over the tragedy
of September 11,

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.820
that we have an opportunity to
have a true soldier of peace

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.060
share his views on the
subject the philosophy

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.130
of conflict resolution.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.190
It is my distinct honor
and happy privilege

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:52.798
to introduce to you
Nobel Laureate John Hume.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:56.291
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDS]

00:04:02.611 --> 00:04:03.277
HUME: Thank you.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.760
Thank you very much.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.280
I'm very pleased to be
with you this evening.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.500
"Lift up your faces.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:19.380
You have a piercing need for
this bright morning dawning

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.079
for you.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:27.270
History, despite its wrenching
pain, cannot be unlived,

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:33.090
and if faced with courage,
need not be lived again."

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.930
These are the words of
the poet Maya Angelou.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.400
They are words of hope.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.420
They are words that
should inspire us all,

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:48.450
at this time of great challenge,
that we must never give up

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.700
the search for a better world.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.400
In the search for an end
to war and suffering,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.090
and in the search for peace and
justice, we shouldn't give up.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.940
Because we're living
at a very historic time

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.450
in the history of the world.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:09.170
We're living one of
the worst centuries

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.000
in the history of the world.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.770
Two world wars.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.075
Millions of people slaughtered.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.786
And, of course,
we're living also

00:05:22.786 --> 00:05:24.660
through the biggest
revolution in the history

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.500
of the word, the technological,
telecommunications,

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.630
and transport revolution.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:34.050
The world is a much smaller
place in your generation

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.390
than it has ever been.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.570
So as we enter in the new
century in a smaller world

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:44.280
and leave behind the
century of two world wars,

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:50.220
let us have our dream,
and work for the dream

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.860
that war and conflict
has been left behind,

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.420
and that we will be building a
new world in which there will

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.500
be total respect for
our common humanity,

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:06.940
and recognize that our
common humanity transcends

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.510
our difference.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.960
It's a great
personal honor for me

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:14.800
to be here this evening
at the Massachusetts

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.210
Institute of Technology to
deliver the Ford Nobel Laureate

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:23.230
Lecture on the theme of
the philosophy of conflict

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.690
resolution.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.960
The people of Boston and
the people of Massachusetts,

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:33.370
and indeed wider America, have
been true and very consistent

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.730
friends of my
country, of Ireland,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.280
and of our peace process.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:44.020
Our shared history and ancestry,
along with the very vibrant

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:47.320
connections that exist
today, provides us

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.700
all with the inspiration we
need to ensure that we will all

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:56.620
enjoy our future, the
limits which are set only

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.200
at the limits of
our own creativity

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.250
and our own imagination.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.980
The great city of
Boston has been

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.290
a true friend of my
own home town of Derry

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.480
through the troubles.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.000
Over the years, we
have made many friends,

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.660
and I have made many friends
in that city, whose support

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.830
and friendship has been
pivotal as I worked

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.420
for economic regeneration
and job creation

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.480
as a very central role
of our peace process.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.090
Because central to
my own philosophy,

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.670
my own political
philosophy, has always

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:38.040
been the belief that by
making real politics work--

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.970
and by real politics
I don't mean

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:42.400
waving flags at one another.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.460
I mean addressing the
real issues of people

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.680
and living standards,
of employment,

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.920
of education, of
housing, of health care.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.130
That we can change the
dynamic of our society

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.720
by concentrating on those,
and transform that society.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.990
All too many young people
from my own city of Derry

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:07.270
and across the north of Ireland
got caught up in paramilitarism

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:11.350
as a consequence of the
crushing unemployment rates that

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:15.310
crippled our prospects
for peace and prosperity,

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.560
because they had no
hope, and discrimination

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.870
was at the heart of it.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:23.110
In an effort to address
that particular problem,

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.540
I was involved in creating
a project that became

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.210
known as Derry-Boston Ventures.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:31.240
Its purpose was to promote
economic development

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.710
between the two cities,
that share so much history.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.659
And with the help of many
of our friends in Boston,

00:08:37.659 --> 00:08:40.179
that became a huge
success, leading

00:08:40.179 --> 00:08:43.210
to the creation
of many new jobs,

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.130
providing many of
our young people

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.220
with hope and prosperity.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.950
As I say, real politics.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.250
Indeed, I believe it's
highly appropriate

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:59.650
that the venue for
this speech is here,

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.250
because Massachusetts
Institute of Technology

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:06.400
is renowned as one of the
leading lights on the world

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.830
stage in education
and technology,

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.770
particularly in
this modern smaller

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.980
world that I'm talking about.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:21.410
And given my commitment again
to developing the IT sector

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.090
in my home city, I
keep telling my people

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.560
that my vision is that the Foyle
Valley, which is our valley,

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.610
should become the
Silicon Valley of Europe,

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.580
allowing the vast potential of
information and communications

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.940
technology to be
fully maximized.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:43.060
Our city Derry has a
youthful, energetic, and very

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.280
well-educated population.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.640
And our university
at Magee College

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.340
has one of the best IT centers
of any college in Ireland.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:56.290
We have a human resource base
there that is second to none,

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.960
and I'm determined that its
full potential be fulfilled

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.650
as part of our peace process
by working closely with you

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.840
people.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.120
And in the intervening
years, of course,

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.490
we have developed
Derry-Boston Ventures.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.890
And it's known as the Derry
Investment Initiative.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.550
And I'm very glad that
one of the leading figures

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:19.930
and chief executive of that body
is with me here this evening.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.490
The support of
those real friends

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:24.130
of Derry here in your
part of the world

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:27.490
has been invaluable
as we have worked

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:31.390
to provide and to
foster new opportunity

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.310
for our young people.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.860
Today, we are closer
than we've ever

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:40.840
been in Ireland to reversing
the historic tide of immigration

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.630
that has brought so many
Irish people to these shores

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:45.430
over many years.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.890
Today, more and more
of our young people

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.340
are thankfully growing
up free from violence,

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:55.180
and able to live and work in
the country of their birth.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:59.020
And today I want to pay tribute
to the people of America

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:03.160
who have stood with us over
those years to get peace,

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.680
and whose help is so central
to building our new society

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.890
in that new Ireland.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.910
Because your country has been a
rock-solid friend of our peace

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:17.620
process in Northern Ireland,
and continues to be.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.390
The support offered
by United States

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:24.230
has been vital as we work to
leave our conflict behind.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.980
Without the United States,
the peace process might never

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:30.160
have succeeded, and
perhaps we may have never

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.380
been able to reach the
historic agreement of Good

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.840
Friday in 1998.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:39.040
For example, our problem,
when you analyze it,

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:42.550
is about three sets
of relationships.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.650
We disagreed about
our relationships

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.010
within Northern Ireland, within
Ireland, and between Ireland

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:49.330
and Britain.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:52.330
Therefore, to solve the problem,
those three relationships

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.970
should be the
agenda at any talks.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:56.800
And that being the
case, the talks

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.690
should be conducted
not by one government

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.117
but by two governments--

00:12:00.117 --> 00:12:02.200
British and Irish governments,
and all the parties

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.460
of Northern Ireland.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:07.730
Now, that's common sense,
and it has happened.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:11.380
But it took a long time
to get two governments

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.810
to agree to work together.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:18.400
Yet, in 1977, the
first statement

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.740
ever made by a president
of the United States

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:24.580
about the Irish problem
was made by Jimmy Carter.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:28.440
And he was strongly advised
to make this statement

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.440
by four people that I'll
talk about in a moment.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.220
But the statement said, called
on the British and Irish

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:36.790
governments to work together to
solve the problem of Northern

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:37.290
Ireland.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.414
And if they did so, they
would get economic support

00:12:39.414 --> 00:12:40.710
from America.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:42.850
Now, that sounds today
a very common sense

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:44.720
and normal statement.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:50.860
But in 1977, it was a very
revolutionary statement.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:55.120
And it finally
happened in 1998, when

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.620
the two governments
and the parties

00:12:56.620 --> 00:13:00.130
could join the table for
the Good Friday Agreement.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:03.790
But Jimmy Carter was persuaded
to say that by four men

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.770
that we called-- that
I worked closely with,

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.230
and they were known
as the four horsemen.

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:09.830
Senator Kennedy.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:14.350
And let me say in this
state that no American has

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:19.030
done more for peace in my
country than your senator.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:22.600
When I was elected as a
very young man in 1970,

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.940
my phone rang.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.010
This is Ted Kennedy.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.540
Could I meet you?

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.422
I want to keep briefed
on your problems.

00:13:30.422 --> 00:13:32.380
Because that's when the
problems were starting.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.820
We met in Germany.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.550
And from then onwards he
kept in regular contact,

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:40.060
kept himself totally
fully informed,

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:42.340
and took necessary initiatives.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:45.560
And of course the late
speaker, Tip O'Neill, who

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:47.490
was a great friend of Ireland.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:52.130
And Hugh Carey of New York,
and Pat Moynihan of New York.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:55.739
And when the two governments
first got together in 1985

00:13:55.739 --> 00:13:57.280
and signed the
Anglo-Irish Agreement,

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.780
the following day my phone rang.

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:01.550
Tip O'Neill.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:05.137
John, we keep our promises--

00:14:05.137 --> 00:14:06.970
having been promised
to economically support

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.830
the governments if
they came together.

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:12.250
We're setting up the
International Fund for Ireland.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.600
That fund has already
created 38,000 jobs

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:19.270
for our young people in
Northern Ireland and the border

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.590
counties.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:25.410
Thank you, Tip O'Neill
and Ted Kennedy.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:33.220
Presently, of course, and
given the situation of course

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.270
that we're in, that
bringing together

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:42.680
people in the economic
scene is part of what

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:45.690
I call the healing process.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.900
But, as I was saying
at the beginning,

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.230
the challenge it now faces
is to leave the conflicts

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:53.900
of past centuries behind us.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.540
And as we enter the new
century and the new millennium,

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:00.400
let us build it as a world of
peace and as regions of peace,

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.540
with no conflict.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.060
Because when you have
a look at conflict,

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:07.900
no matter where it is--

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.570
and this is me
talking very simply,

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.080
but I think it's
also quite profound--

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:15.170
all conflict is about the same
thing no matter where it is.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:18.830
It's about difference,
whether difference

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:25.280
is your religion, or your
race, or your nationality.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:27.090
And the message that
we have to get across

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:30.356
and that we have learned
in our part of the world

00:15:30.356 --> 00:15:33.830
is that difference is
an accident of birth.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:36.470
None of us chose to be born.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.270
And we certainly didn't
choose to be born

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.630
into any particular community.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:46.250
There's not two people in
this hall who are the same.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.200
There's not two people in the
whole world who are the same.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.750
Difference is at the
essence of humanity,

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:58.480
and therefore respect
for difference

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:02.050
should be very, very
normal and very common.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:07.060
But it is the first and
deepest principle of real peace

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.880
and real ending of conflict.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:14.450
And look at our conflict
in Northern Ireland

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.790
over the past 30 years.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:20.240
With a population of
a million and a half,

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:30.320
3,700 people lost their lives or
killed, one out of 450 people.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:34.640
That's the equivalent
of half a million people

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:38.330
being killed in the United
States in percentage terms.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.940
That's how serious it was.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:44.220
And, of course, in
addition to that,

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:47.480
over 40,000 people were
maimed and injured.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:52.990
That's one out of 50 people.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:56.890
That's the equivalent of 5
million people in the United

00:16:56.890 --> 00:17:00.230
States being maimed or injured.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:04.210
That's how serious
our conflict has been,

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:10.130
and therefore how difficult
it was to bring it to an end.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.795
And it was also necessary
because of that,

00:17:12.795 --> 00:17:18.349
in the highest churchgoing
city in Europe, Belfast,

00:17:18.349 --> 00:17:25.900
to build walls, up to 12
walls, to separate and protect

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:30.540
one section of a Christian
people from another.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:35.830
I always described those walls
as an indictment of all of us,

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:40.410
because, as I said, our past
attitudes had built them.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.110
And for that reason, we should
regard them as a challenge

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:49.810
to us, a challenge to
change our past attitudes.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:54.030
And when you look at our past
attitudes, or our mentalities,

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:57.840
you'll find those
mentalities also exist

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:01.370
in most areas of conflict.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.679
There is the mentality
of the unionist people

00:18:03.679 --> 00:18:05.220
in Northern Ireland,
who were largely

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.600
the Protestant population.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.620
And I called that the
Afrikaner mindset,

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:13.320
the Afrikaner mentality.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.200
They wished to protect
their identity,

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.540
and they rightly wished
to protect their identity

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.690
within Ireland.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:24.870
And I would have no quarrel with
that because it's, as I say,

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.500
diversity enriches society.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.630
And therefore it's
right that they should

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.790
wish to protect their identity.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:37.470
My quarrel with them was
their method of protecting it,

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.020
the Afrikaner method,
as I called it, holding

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:43.112
all power in their own hands.

00:18:43.112 --> 00:18:44.820
In other words, if
you weren't a unionist

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.540
in Northern Ireland
when we were growing up,

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.140
you had great difficulty.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.350
You never would be in power of
any description in politics,

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:55.320
but you also would have great
difficulty in getting a job,

00:18:55.320 --> 00:19:00.500
or getting a house, or
even getting a vote.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:05.270
Voting was given to
only those people

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:08.680
who paid rates and rents.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.180
And when I would be growing up,
if I had been of voting age,

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.221
the only people who would
have votes in the house

00:19:13.221 --> 00:19:15.800
would be the father and mother.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.770
And if you owned a company,
a business company,

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:21.620
each business company
had six votes.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.540
And when I was young,
the mayor of Derry

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:29.240
had 43 votes because he owned
seven companies, each of which

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:32.150
had six votes,
plus his own vote.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.760
And, of course, we suffered
terrible discrimination

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:36.980
in jobs and housing.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.440
And although they were
only 30% of the population,

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:43.080
the unionists ruled the city
by a system of gerrymander.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.470
That was the Afrikaner mindset.

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:50.080
Our challenge to that was,
discrimination of that nature

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:53.120
will, in the end,
only lead to conflict,

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:56.540
and it's not the correct way
to protect your identity.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.060
And my challenge to them was,
because of your geography

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.310
and your numbers in
Northern Ireland,

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.350
the problem can't be
solved without you.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.980
Therefore, come to
the table and reach

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:11.660
an agreement that will
protect your identity forever.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:14.000
In other words, dialogue.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.430
And dialogue is central to a
peace process in any divided

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.024
society.

00:20:19.024 --> 00:20:20.690
Then, of course, there
was the mentality

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:23.400
of my own community,
what's called

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:27.230
the nationalist mentality,
or the nationalist mindset.

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:31.050
And, of course, I
challenged that as well.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:34.370
I called that the
territorial mindset.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.910
Ireland is our land.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.140
Your union is a
minority in our land

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.985
and you can't stop us uniting.

00:20:41.985 --> 00:20:43.610
And of course there's
a lot of quarrels

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:46.640
in the world about
land and territory.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:50.610
But my challenge to that mindset
was, look, hold on a minute

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:51.110
here.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:55.280
It's people that have
rights, not territory.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:59.660
Without people, even Ireland,
our beautiful Ireland,

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.360
is only a jungle.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:07.280
And when people are divided,
as they are in Ireland,

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:12.860
they can never be brought
together with guns and bombs.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:18.350
Division can only be
deepened by guns and bombs,

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:22.590
and the problem made far
more difficult to solve.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:27.690
And, of course, if one
side uses guns and bombs,

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:30.830
the other replies
with guns and bombs.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:36.220
And, as Martin Luther King and
Mahatma Gandhi kept repeating,

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:40.820
and we did as well, the old
doctrine of an eye for an eye

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.290
leaves everybody blind.

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:46.070
Violence, in other
words, had no role

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:49.550
to play in solving our problem.

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:55.970
And, of course, given that we
are a divided people and not

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:59.360
a divided piece of
earth, once again

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:02.990
the only solution is
agreement, and getting together

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:06.240
in dialogue to reach
that agreement.

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:09.860
So the challenge to
both mentalities,

00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:13.580
as I have made clear in my
few words recently to you,

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:17.000
was to come to the table
and reach agreement

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:20.730
as to how to share the
piece of earth together.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:24.390
And, of course,
that wasn't easy.

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:26.870
But we eventually succeeded.

00:22:26.870 --> 00:22:31.810
And I have to admit that, in
my work as a political leader

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:35.360
in working for that
agreement and getting

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:37.700
the violence stopped
on our streets,

00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:41.450
I was very heavily inspired
by my European experience,

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:43.700
because I'm a member of the
European Parliament, where

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:46.320
I have been since 1979.

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:51.050
And when I first went there--
and I always tell this story--

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.450
when I first went to Strasbourg
to a European Parliament

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:58.580
meeting in 1979,
I went for a walk.

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:00.560
And I crossed the
bridge from Strasbourg,

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:05.170
which is in France, to
Kehl, which is in Germany.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:09.370
And I stopped and I
thought, good lord.

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:12.430
If I had stood in this
bridge 30 years ago,

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:18.520
1949, just after the Second
World War, 35 million people

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:20.440
slaughtered.

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:26.500
And if I had said, don't
worry, it's all over,

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:32.190
and in 20 years' time
we'll have a united Europe.

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.560
The quarrel will be
over, and the French

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:38.640
will still be French, and the
Germans will still be German.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.870
I said to myself, if I had
thought that 30 years ago, I

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:44.910
would have been sent
to a psychiatrist.

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.470
But it happened.

00:23:47.470 --> 00:23:51.060
And the European Union,
when you think of it today,

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:53.250
is the best example in
the history of the world

00:23:53.250 --> 00:23:55.670
of conflict resolution.

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:58.550
And for that reason, the
principles and philosophy

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:01.640
at the heart of it
should be studied

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:05.590
by every area of
conflict and brought

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:08.320
to every area of conflict.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:11.020
And when you look
at the principles,

00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:13.280
they're simple and
straightforward.

00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:16.570
The first principle, as
I've talked about already,

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:20.410
was respect for difference.

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:23.800
Because what was our wars about?

00:24:23.800 --> 00:24:26.590
And respect for difference
is a fundamental principle

00:24:26.590 --> 00:24:27.400
of European Union.

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:30.110
No victory for any country.

00:24:30.110 --> 00:24:31.730
Second principle.

00:24:31.730 --> 00:24:36.350
Creating institutions which
respected those differences,

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:39.470
a council of
ministers which meets,

00:24:39.470 --> 00:24:43.090
and there's a minister
from every country.

00:24:43.090 --> 00:24:46.920
And no matter how small or large
the country is, none of them

00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:49.440
can dominate the others.

00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:52.420
They work by agreement.

00:24:52.420 --> 00:24:57.010
And the second institution
is the European Commission,

00:24:57.010 --> 00:24:59.950
which is a civil service
of European Union, drawn

00:24:59.950 --> 00:25:03.260
from all member countries.

00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:06.380
And the third is a
European Parliament, drawn

00:25:06.380 --> 00:25:09.510
from all member countries.

00:25:09.510 --> 00:25:12.342
No victories for any,
but they're all there.

00:25:12.342 --> 00:25:13.800
And then the third
principle, which

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:17.770
is the most important
principle of all, which is what

00:25:17.770 --> 00:25:21.190
I call the healing process.

00:25:21.190 --> 00:25:25.780
They work together in
their common interests,

00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:30.660
which was largely economics,
the areas of agreement.

00:25:30.660 --> 00:25:32.910
They spilt their sweat,
as I always say, and not

00:25:32.910 --> 00:25:35.850
their blood, and
by working together

00:25:35.850 --> 00:25:40.530
in their common interests, broke
down the barriers of centuries.

00:25:40.530 --> 00:25:46.970
And the new Europe has
evolved, and is still evolving.

00:25:46.970 --> 00:25:49.640
And although it only started
out with six countries,

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.990
there's now 15 there.

00:25:52.990 --> 00:25:56.380
Those same principles
are at the heart

00:25:56.380 --> 00:26:00.130
of our agreement of
Good Friday in Ireland,

00:26:00.130 --> 00:26:01.310
when you look at it.

00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:05.320
Principle number one,
respect for difference.

00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:09.010
There was no victory for either
community in our agreement.

00:26:09.010 --> 00:26:11.230
Total respect for the
unionist identity.

00:26:11.230 --> 00:26:14.910
Total respect for the
nationalist identity.

00:26:14.910 --> 00:26:16.470
Second principle.

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:21.600
Institutions which
respected those differences.

00:26:21.600 --> 00:26:23.570
An assembly elected
to Northern Ireland

00:26:23.570 --> 00:26:27.730
by a voting system of
proportional representation,

00:26:27.730 --> 00:26:30.850
which ensures that all
sections of the people

00:26:30.850 --> 00:26:34.450
are totally democratically
represented.

00:26:34.450 --> 00:26:36.280
And then that assembly
proportionally

00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:39.790
elects the government
or executive,

00:26:39.790 --> 00:26:44.580
and all sections are
represented in the government.

00:26:44.580 --> 00:26:48.300
And then the third
principle of course,

00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:52.290
which is the most important,
is that our representatives

00:26:52.290 --> 00:26:54.480
from all sections
of our community

00:26:54.480 --> 00:27:00.540
work together in our common
interests, economic growth.

00:27:00.540 --> 00:27:03.070
Spill our sweat, not our blood.

00:27:03.070 --> 00:27:06.850
And that's the real
healing process,

00:27:06.850 --> 00:27:09.920
working our common
ground together.

00:27:09.920 --> 00:27:13.450
And as we do so, as we spill
our sweat and not our blood,

00:27:13.450 --> 00:27:16.240
break down the
barriers of centuries

00:27:16.240 --> 00:27:19.330
of distrust and prejudice.

00:27:19.330 --> 00:27:23.950
And the new Ireland will
evolve in a generation or two

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:28.180
based on agreement and
respect for difference.

00:27:28.180 --> 00:27:31.000
And, indeed, I come back to the
importance of the United States

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:34.570
in that healing process area.

00:27:34.570 --> 00:27:37.180
Because, given that
the healing process

00:27:37.180 --> 00:27:40.460
is working the common
ground together,

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:44.070
the economic development,
wiping out unemployment

00:27:44.070 --> 00:27:45.900
and giving real hope
to our young people

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:49.630
that they can earn a living
in the land of their birth,

00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:52.500
United States has a very
important role to play in that,

00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:54.550
and already are playing it.

00:27:54.550 --> 00:27:59.410
So, as I said earlier, when our
four horsemen friends set up

00:27:59.410 --> 00:28:02.720
the International
Fund for Ireland.

00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:06.970
But, in addition to that,
American investment.

00:28:06.970 --> 00:28:08.980
And of course the
marketing of the products

00:28:08.980 --> 00:28:12.580
of our small industries
in the United States.

00:28:12.580 --> 00:28:15.070
And of course, in
recent times, we've

00:28:15.070 --> 00:28:18.190
been very fortunate,
again in my own city,

00:28:18.190 --> 00:28:20.510
in attracting major
American investments.

00:28:20.510 --> 00:28:25.030
My city is now the European
headquarters of DuPont,

00:28:25.030 --> 00:28:30.190
Fruit of the Loom, Seagate,
Stream International.

00:28:30.190 --> 00:28:34.370
And under their roofs, young
people from both communities

00:28:34.370 --> 00:28:36.510
are working together.

00:28:36.510 --> 00:28:39.500
And as they work together,
our dream and hope

00:28:39.500 --> 00:28:42.080
is, of course, that
we will break down

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:47.210
the barriers of the past
and that trust will grow,

00:28:47.210 --> 00:28:51.830
and the new Ireland will evolve
based on agreement and respect

00:28:51.830 --> 00:28:54.300
for difference.

00:28:54.300 --> 00:28:56.980
And let me say to you now--

00:28:56.980 --> 00:29:00.000
and I'm sure that many of
you have forgotten it--

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.600
the philosophy that I am
talking to you about tonight

00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:07.300
is a philosophy that you'll
find in your country.

00:29:07.300 --> 00:29:11.350
And you will find it summarized
if you pull a cent out

00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:14.620
of your pocket and read it.

00:29:14.620 --> 00:29:16.770
Because there it is written.

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:20.146
And I learned about it by
studying your history as well.

00:29:20.146 --> 00:29:21.820
The three words.

00:29:21.820 --> 00:29:24.480
And if you can't, if your
eyesight is not good enough

00:29:24.480 --> 00:29:28.380
to read the cent, go to the
grave of Abraham Lincoln,

00:29:28.380 --> 00:29:30.620
and there you will
see the message.

00:29:30.620 --> 00:29:33.450
"E pluribus unum."

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:36.310
From many we are one.

00:29:36.310 --> 00:29:41.560
The essence of our unity is
respect for our diversity.

00:29:41.560 --> 00:29:44.470
The real philosophy of peace--

00:29:44.470 --> 00:29:47.430
respect for difference.

00:29:47.430 --> 00:29:49.170
Look at the whole human race.

00:29:49.170 --> 00:29:53.310
As I said earlier, humanity
transcends nationality.

00:29:53.310 --> 00:29:56.910
Humanity transcends race
and religion, et cetera.

00:29:56.910 --> 00:29:59.750
First and foremost,
we're human beings.

00:29:59.750 --> 00:30:01.410
And our common
humanity therefore

00:30:01.410 --> 00:30:07.170
demands that we
respect our diversity.

00:30:07.170 --> 00:30:11.380
And when I was awarded the
Nobel Peace Prize in '98,

00:30:11.380 --> 00:30:14.440
I quoted the Irish poet
William Butler Yeats,

00:30:14.440 --> 00:30:21.140
who said, "Too long a sacrifice
can make a stone of the heart,"

00:30:21.140 --> 00:30:24.060
if your troubles go on so long.

00:30:24.060 --> 00:30:26.560
And there have been times
during the last 30 years

00:30:26.560 --> 00:30:30.040
in Northern Ireland when
the search for peace

00:30:30.040 --> 00:30:32.520
may have seemed futile.

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:36.760
At the start, a cycle of
violence and counterviolence,

00:30:36.760 --> 00:30:40.810
and political failure, that
led to so much devastation

00:30:40.810 --> 00:30:41.910
on our streets.

00:30:41.910 --> 00:30:45.270
There was despair that
it could never end.

00:30:45.270 --> 00:30:47.660
But a well-known Belfast
writer, CS Lewis,

00:30:47.660 --> 00:30:53.090
once said that, "Between no
hope and very little hope,

00:30:53.090 --> 00:30:56.280
lies a vast ocean
of possibility."

00:30:56.280 --> 00:30:58.500
In other words,
always be positive.

00:30:58.500 --> 00:31:00.990
Look for the positive
and not the negative.

00:31:00.990 --> 00:31:02.560
He was right.

00:31:02.560 --> 00:31:06.390
In Northern Ireland, there
always has been hope.

00:31:06.390 --> 00:31:09.360
Ordinary people never
lost faith that a new road

00:31:09.360 --> 00:31:11.270
could be traveled.

00:31:11.270 --> 00:31:16.040
On Good Friday in 1998,
the political parties

00:31:16.040 --> 00:31:20.910
of all of the north of Ireland
agreed to walk a new road.

00:31:20.910 --> 00:31:26.340
We chose the way of peace, of
partnership, of opportunity.

00:31:26.340 --> 00:31:29.700
And the people of Ireland,
north and south, opted

00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:33.030
to walk that new
road with us, because

00:31:33.030 --> 00:31:36.460
for the first time
in our history--

00:31:36.460 --> 00:31:39.390
and this is rather surprising it
was the first time in history--

00:31:39.390 --> 00:31:41.970
the people of
Ireland as a whole,

00:31:41.970 --> 00:31:44.580
north and south,
spoke as to how they

00:31:44.580 --> 00:31:47.640
wish to share the piece
of earth together,

00:31:47.640 --> 00:31:50.340
when they came in the joint
referendum, north and south

00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:54.000
on the one day, and
overwhelmingly voted

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:57.070
for the Good Friday Agreement.

00:31:57.070 --> 00:32:00.180
And that now makes it the
duty of all true democrats

00:32:00.180 --> 00:32:03.589
in Ireland to implement
the will of the people.

00:32:03.589 --> 00:32:05.130
And those minorities
that are seeking

00:32:05.130 --> 00:32:08.050
to overthrow the
agreement are working

00:32:08.050 --> 00:32:12.010
against the will of the people.

00:32:12.010 --> 00:32:15.575
There's one of them who's a very
leading clerical politician.

00:32:15.575 --> 00:32:17.700
And I said to him, Ian, if
you took the word no out

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:20.680
of the English language,
you would be speechless.

00:32:20.680 --> 00:32:22.221
And he says, no I wouldn't.

00:32:22.221 --> 00:32:25.660
[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

00:32:25.660 --> 00:32:30.470
But in spite of our
progress, today, more than 3

00:32:30.470 --> 00:32:34.240
and 1/2 years later, we
appear to have only traveled

00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:36.100
a short distance.

00:32:36.100 --> 00:32:39.310
But although it is a
short distance, given

00:32:39.310 --> 00:32:44.930
our past number of
centuries of conflict,

00:32:44.930 --> 00:32:47.420
it's quite a distance.

00:32:47.420 --> 00:32:50.130
And that's the nature
of conflict resolution.

00:32:50.130 --> 00:32:53.600
There are no easy answers,
or no quick-fix solutions.

00:32:53.600 --> 00:32:56.870
It's a tough and
difficult process.

00:32:56.870 --> 00:33:01.370
And, of course, as I've said,
it will take the healing process

00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:02.810
to complete it.

00:33:02.810 --> 00:33:04.490
But we will not give it up.

00:33:04.490 --> 00:33:06.680
And we owe it to the
people of our country

00:33:06.680 --> 00:33:09.140
and to the wider
world, as I have said,

00:33:09.140 --> 00:33:12.130
to keep moving forward.

00:33:12.130 --> 00:33:15.250
Because when you have the
divisions of centuries,

00:33:15.250 --> 00:33:18.710
as we have and as most
areas of conflict have,

00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:21.520
you don't heal them in
a week or a fortnight.

00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:25.510
It requires the healing
process, the spilling of sweat

00:33:25.510 --> 00:33:28.440
and not of blood,
the working together

00:33:28.440 --> 00:33:30.640
in the common interests.

00:33:30.640 --> 00:33:33.260
And that's what
we are now doing.

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:36.510
And there's no doubt at all
that our people in Ireland

00:33:36.510 --> 00:33:39.490
have set out on an
irreversible course

00:33:39.490 --> 00:33:41.940
towards a peaceful future.

00:33:41.940 --> 00:33:45.340
The commitment exists to ensure
that we create a future where

00:33:45.340 --> 00:33:50.080
everyone can enjoy equal and
fundamental human rights,

00:33:50.080 --> 00:33:53.470
where every young Irish
person can find work and enjoy

00:33:53.470 --> 00:33:56.170
a good quality of
life, where the pursuit

00:33:56.170 --> 00:34:00.040
of our common interest is
the most potent expression

00:34:00.040 --> 00:34:02.740
of our shared patriotism.

00:34:02.740 --> 00:34:05.350
The fundamental implementation,
therefore, of the Good Friday

00:34:05.350 --> 00:34:10.330
Agreement is the vehicle for
delivering that new Ireland,

00:34:10.330 --> 00:34:12.550
in which Catholic,
Protestant, and Dissenter will

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:16.861
live together in equality
and respect for diversity.

00:34:16.861 --> 00:34:23.090
And the time has now come for
the world as well to learn.

00:34:23.090 --> 00:34:25.880
And as I've already said,
and I keep repeating,

00:34:25.880 --> 00:34:27.800
because it's a time
to make people think,

00:34:27.800 --> 00:34:31.940
I think, that we and you,
you are the generation that

00:34:31.940 --> 00:34:35.850
will be leading in the new
century and the new millennium.

00:34:35.850 --> 00:34:41.489
So the challenge is to make
sure that your influence is

00:34:41.489 --> 00:34:46.590
used to ensure that the entire
world learns that humanity

00:34:46.590 --> 00:34:51.000
transcends difference,
that difference is indeed

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:54.420
the very essence of humanity.

00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:58.770
Let them learn the fundamental
of your constitution,

00:34:58.770 --> 00:35:00.580
"E pluribus unum."

00:35:00.580 --> 00:35:02.530
From many we are one.

00:35:02.530 --> 00:35:05.800
Its message is very clear,
and it's a powerful message

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:07.880
of peace for the world.

00:35:07.880 --> 00:35:10.240
Diversity is a good thing.

00:35:10.240 --> 00:35:12.810
Diversity is a healthy thing.

00:35:12.810 --> 00:35:16.130
Diversity enriches the world.

00:35:16.130 --> 00:35:19.430
No longer can it be
allowed to drive us apart.

00:35:19.430 --> 00:35:21.950
No longer can it be
allowed to perpetuate

00:35:21.950 --> 00:35:25.190
sterile and bloody conflict.

00:35:25.190 --> 00:35:28.040
Instead, the true
potential of diversity

00:35:28.040 --> 00:35:30.530
must be fostered
as a valuable tool

00:35:30.530 --> 00:35:35.090
for bringing people together,
for promoting reconciliation

00:35:35.090 --> 00:35:40.250
and developing new and dynamic
relationships between peoples.

00:35:40.250 --> 00:35:45.530
In short, as I made clear, no
two human beings are the same,

00:35:45.530 --> 00:35:48.500
and humanity is richer
for that difference.

00:35:48.500 --> 00:35:50.720
Where would we be, and
what sort of a world

00:35:50.720 --> 00:35:54.680
would it be, if we
were all the same?

00:35:54.680 --> 00:35:57.080
The answer to difference
is to respect it

00:35:57.080 --> 00:36:01.040
and not to fight about
it, to live for ideals,

00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:07.540
to live for your country, rather
than to die or kill for it.

00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:10.090
And as we begin the
new century, the time

00:36:10.090 --> 00:36:14.080
has come for us all to
respect our common humanity.

00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:16.480
The time has come for
us all to commit fully

00:36:16.480 --> 00:36:19.090
to achieving the end
of all conflict--

00:36:19.090 --> 00:36:22.645
because the victims of conflict,
no matter where they are,

00:36:22.645 --> 00:36:24.850
are human beings--

00:36:24.850 --> 00:36:26.890
and to apply the
basic principles

00:36:26.890 --> 00:36:30.920
of conflict resolution
to all areas of conflict.

00:36:30.920 --> 00:36:34.910
In short, the time for a
peaceful world has arrived.

00:36:34.910 --> 00:36:36.320
In the words of
President John F.

00:36:36.320 --> 00:36:40.850
Kennedy, spoken
in 1963 but still

00:36:40.850 --> 00:36:43.776
as relevant today as then--

00:36:43.776 --> 00:36:46.500
and listen to what he said--

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:51.100
"We can help make the
world safe for diversity.

00:36:51.100 --> 00:36:55.210
For in the final analysis,
our most basic common link

00:36:55.210 --> 00:37:00.310
is that we all inhabit
this small planet.

00:37:00.310 --> 00:37:03.280
We all breathe the same air.

00:37:03.280 --> 00:37:06.610
We all cherish our
children's future.

00:37:06.610 --> 00:37:09.840
And we are all mortal."

00:37:09.840 --> 00:37:12.670
Let us now seek out that
way of peace and justice

00:37:12.670 --> 00:37:13.875
for all the world.

00:37:13.875 --> 00:37:19.570
And when you think of
those words in 1963

00:37:19.570 --> 00:37:22.330
about this small
planet, the planet today

00:37:22.330 --> 00:37:24.870
is even much smaller.

00:37:24.870 --> 00:37:28.690
Therefore, the challenge that
President Kennedy put to us

00:37:28.690 --> 00:37:31.880
is much, much
clearer and stronger.

00:37:31.880 --> 00:37:35.720
And let us make it our
dream and our ideal

00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:38.690
that the new century
and a new millennium

00:37:38.690 --> 00:37:41.630
will be a new century
and a new millennium

00:37:41.630 --> 00:37:45.650
where e pluribus unum
will be the principle

00:37:45.650 --> 00:37:48.130
of the whole world
and the whole planet.

00:37:48.130 --> 00:37:49.446
Thank you.

00:37:49.446 --> 00:37:52.897
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDS]

00:37:55.189 --> 00:37:55.855
CLAY: Thank you.

00:37:55.855 --> 00:37:56.973
Your speech was very good.

00:37:56.973 --> 00:37:59.306
Why don't you just stay and
we'll accept some questions.

00:37:59.306 --> 00:38:02.757
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDS]

00:38:19.560 --> 00:38:21.920
Dr. Hume will accept
some questions.

00:38:21.920 --> 00:38:24.840
There are mics in
several places.

00:38:29.990 --> 00:38:30.720
Yes.

00:38:30.720 --> 00:38:32.570
AUDIENCE: Hello.

00:38:32.570 --> 00:38:37.107
Dr. Hume, as a young person from
west Belfast, Northern Ireland,

00:38:37.107 --> 00:38:38.690
I'd just like to
take this opportunity

00:38:38.690 --> 00:38:40.850
to say thank you to you.

00:38:40.850 --> 00:38:42.710
I know that without
your outstanding work

00:38:42.710 --> 00:38:46.190
over the last 30 years,
people like myself would never

00:38:46.190 --> 00:38:49.740
have had the opportunity to
have a university education,

00:38:49.740 --> 00:38:51.920
to have a vote, and
also for me to be

00:38:51.920 --> 00:38:55.190
able to say that I count the
daughter of Lord Taylor as one

00:38:55.190 --> 00:38:56.910
of my good friends.

00:38:56.910 --> 00:38:59.000
However, I'm also
very concerned by

00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:02.510
the current political climate
at the moment, the continuing

00:39:02.510 --> 00:39:06.210
protests in Ardoyne at the
Catholic school, the breakdown

00:39:06.210 --> 00:39:09.560
of the loyalist ceasefires,
and the recent revelation

00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:12.500
that unionist politicians
have been speaking

00:39:12.500 --> 00:39:15.890
to loyalist paramilitaries,
while at the same time

00:39:15.890 --> 00:39:17.630
trying to bring
down the Assembly

00:39:17.630 --> 00:39:20.360
and refusing to sit in
power with Sinn Fein.

00:39:20.360 --> 00:39:23.360
I'm just wondering
how you perceive

00:39:23.360 --> 00:39:27.210
the situation developing
over the next few years.

00:39:27.210 --> 00:39:32.300
HUME: Well, as I said earlier,
we have come 3 and 1/2 years,

00:39:32.300 --> 00:39:36.980
and it's not as far as we
want to come but we have

00:39:36.980 --> 00:39:39.560
made considerable progress.

00:39:39.560 --> 00:39:42.600
As I say, the vast
majority of our streets,

00:39:42.600 --> 00:39:44.660
there is peace in our
streets and the atmosphere

00:39:44.660 --> 00:39:46.160
has been transformed.

00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:49.420
But there have been some
recent difficulties.

00:39:49.420 --> 00:39:51.660
And one of the
difficulties, of course,

00:39:51.660 --> 00:39:55.580
relates to the implementation
of the agreement.

00:39:55.580 --> 00:39:57.730
And the point that has
to be made about that,

00:39:57.730 --> 00:40:00.680
which I have already
made, is that it

00:40:00.680 --> 00:40:03.810
is the will of the people.

00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:07.290
That because when the agreement
was reached, my party proposed,

00:40:07.290 --> 00:40:10.470
I proposed that the last
word would be with the people

00:40:10.470 --> 00:40:13.850
and not with the
politicians, so that nobody,

00:40:13.850 --> 00:40:15.890
once the agreement
was put into place,

00:40:15.890 --> 00:40:17.810
could then oppose
it and claim they

00:40:17.810 --> 00:40:20.006
were acting in the
name of the people.

00:40:20.006 --> 00:40:21.630
The people overwhelmingly
voted for it.

00:40:21.630 --> 00:40:23.360
Therefore, it's our
duty to implement it.

00:40:23.360 --> 00:40:26.180
Therefore, the one area of
controversy at the minute

00:40:26.180 --> 00:40:28.070
to be implemented
is what's called

00:40:28.070 --> 00:40:30.450
the decommissioning area.

00:40:30.450 --> 00:40:34.640
In other words, the paramilitary
organizations like the IRA

00:40:34.640 --> 00:40:37.940
should, with the International
Commission General de

00:40:37.940 --> 00:40:40.040
Chastelain-- nobody's
asking them to surrender,

00:40:40.040 --> 00:40:42.170
but they should show the
International Commission

00:40:42.170 --> 00:40:44.750
that their guns have
been put beyond use.

00:40:44.750 --> 00:40:47.480
They should do that
as soon as possible,

00:40:47.480 --> 00:40:49.630
and that will transform
the atmosphere.

00:40:49.630 --> 00:40:51.350
And I hope that they will do so.

00:40:51.350 --> 00:40:54.530
Secondly, David
Trimble and company

00:40:54.530 --> 00:40:59.240
should not be talking
about withdrawing

00:40:59.240 --> 00:41:02.030
from the institutions
like the executive,

00:41:02.030 --> 00:41:04.420
as you have said
they are now doing.

00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:06.950
Because there again,
what they're doing

00:41:06.950 --> 00:41:10.940
is working to bring down the
agreement that the people have

00:41:10.940 --> 00:41:13.670
overwhelmingly voted for.

00:41:13.670 --> 00:41:17.540
And, of course, there
is also certain elements

00:41:17.540 --> 00:41:19.640
in paramilitary
organizations who

00:41:19.640 --> 00:41:23.390
are trying to keep
the troubles going.

00:41:23.390 --> 00:41:25.400
And north Belfast you mentioned.

00:41:25.400 --> 00:41:28.055
And my belief is
that what's happening

00:41:28.055 --> 00:41:29.840
there is there are
certain elements

00:41:29.840 --> 00:41:32.990
in paramilitary organizations
who don't want law and order

00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:36.380
or peace in our streets,
because they want to keep up

00:41:36.380 --> 00:41:39.860
their mafia work
in the drugs trade,

00:41:39.860 --> 00:41:42.530
and it's not about politics.

00:41:42.530 --> 00:41:44.720
And therefore the
whole community

00:41:44.720 --> 00:41:48.650
should unite totally and
absolutely against them

00:41:48.650 --> 00:41:51.750
in order to get that stopped.

00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:53.600
And I know nothing,
strangely enough--

00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:55.910
and I'm sure you'll
all agree with me--

00:41:55.910 --> 00:41:58.730
I know nothing in
the whole 30 years

00:41:58.730 --> 00:42:03.380
in Northern Ireland that got
as much international publicity

00:42:03.380 --> 00:42:05.510
as those children
being stopped going

00:42:05.510 --> 00:42:08.550
to school in north Belfast.

00:42:08.550 --> 00:42:10.670
And when it started,
I was in Strasbourg

00:42:10.670 --> 00:42:13.450
at the European Parliament, and
it had never happened before.

00:42:13.450 --> 00:42:15.830
But my colleagues from
Germany, and France,

00:42:15.830 --> 00:42:18.430
and Spain, and Italy were
all walking up to me.

00:42:18.430 --> 00:42:21.560
John, what is wrong?

00:42:21.560 --> 00:42:24.290
What sort of people are
that who are stopping

00:42:24.290 --> 00:42:27.250
your kids from going to school?

00:42:27.250 --> 00:42:29.330
And of course I went on
the radio and television

00:42:29.330 --> 00:42:32.090
immediately to
Belfast to say, I'm

00:42:32.090 --> 00:42:34.280
speaking to the
Protestant people.

00:42:34.280 --> 00:42:36.101
The image that's
going out to the world

00:42:36.101 --> 00:42:37.850
is that the Protestant
people are stopping

00:42:37.850 --> 00:42:39.830
these children going to school.

00:42:39.830 --> 00:42:41.707
And I know that
that is not correct,

00:42:41.707 --> 00:42:43.790
because the vast majority
of the Protestant people

00:42:43.790 --> 00:42:46.110
are not involved in this.

00:42:46.110 --> 00:42:48.020
There's a certain
minority involved.

00:42:48.020 --> 00:42:51.050
Therefore I called on the
Protestant church leaders

00:42:51.050 --> 00:42:53.840
and politicians to come
out and condemn it.

00:42:53.840 --> 00:42:56.910
And they have come out and made
clear their opposition to it.

00:42:56.910 --> 00:42:59.540
And we have been
working to get meetings

00:42:59.540 --> 00:43:02.360
between the residents
and the schools

00:43:02.360 --> 00:43:04.670
to get the matter resolved.

00:43:04.670 --> 00:43:07.220
But, as I said, there's those
who are trying to stir it up,

00:43:07.220 --> 00:43:09.050
but I hope we will
get it resolved.

00:43:09.050 --> 00:43:15.080
But, as I say, when you're
ending centuries of conflict,

00:43:15.080 --> 00:43:19.550
you don't get rid
of the distrusts

00:43:19.550 --> 00:43:22.310
at the heart of the division
in a week or a fortnight.

00:43:22.310 --> 00:43:24.770
It does require the
healing process,

00:43:24.770 --> 00:43:26.900
and the framework for
our healing process

00:43:26.900 --> 00:43:30.590
are our new institutions,
and we must preserve those.

00:43:34.240 --> 00:43:36.400
CURHAN: Mr. Hume, my
name is Jared Curhan.

00:43:36.400 --> 00:43:39.220
I'm on the faculty
at the Sloan School,

00:43:39.220 --> 00:43:41.440
where I teach negotiation.

00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:43.810
I realize this
question may be outside

00:43:43.810 --> 00:43:46.510
of your immediate
expertise, but given

00:43:46.510 --> 00:43:49.390
that the title of your talk
is the philosophy of conflict

00:43:49.390 --> 00:43:53.620
resolution, I wanted to
ask you to comment briefly

00:43:53.620 --> 00:43:57.130
on the current situation
between the United States

00:43:57.130 --> 00:43:59.190
and the war on terrorism.

00:43:59.190 --> 00:44:02.410
Specifically, President
Bush was quoted recently

00:44:02.410 --> 00:44:06.970
as rejecting what may or may
not have been a serious offer

00:44:06.970 --> 00:44:09.970
by the Taliban for negotiation.

00:44:09.970 --> 00:44:13.720
And I'm curious as to what
you think about that stance

00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:19.790
and how your three principles
might apply to this conflict.

00:44:19.790 --> 00:44:21.550
HUME: Well, first
of all, I think

00:44:21.550 --> 00:44:26.860
that the terrible atrocities
committed in New York

00:44:26.860 --> 00:44:32.660
and Washington had great
sympathy right across the world

00:44:32.660 --> 00:44:34.690
with the American people,
and there's absolutely

00:44:34.690 --> 00:44:36.185
no doubt about that.

00:44:36.185 --> 00:44:37.810
And I have no doubt
either that there's

00:44:37.810 --> 00:44:41.327
strong unity across
the democratic world

00:44:41.327 --> 00:44:42.910
that all democratic
governments should

00:44:42.910 --> 00:44:46.250
get together with the
United States administration

00:44:46.250 --> 00:44:47.770
and to do everything
in their power

00:44:47.770 --> 00:44:51.340
to bring to justice
the individuals

00:44:51.340 --> 00:44:55.990
and organizations that
committed those atrocities.

00:44:55.990 --> 00:45:00.630
But in so doing, to ensure
and to do everything

00:45:00.630 --> 00:45:03.375
in their power to ensure that
innocent people don't suffer.

00:45:03.375 --> 00:45:04.750
Because that's
one of the dangers

00:45:04.750 --> 00:45:07.870
of this type of situation,
that if innocent people suffer,

00:45:07.870 --> 00:45:13.000
it creates more recruitment for
the terrorist organizations.

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:17.140
But the other thing that I
would like them to do as well

00:45:17.140 --> 00:45:23.530
is to ask for the reasons
why those people did that,

00:45:23.530 --> 00:45:25.450
to find out why did they do it.

00:45:25.450 --> 00:45:29.240
Because, quite often
in terrorist activity,

00:45:29.240 --> 00:45:30.880
the terrorists who
are engaged in it

00:45:30.880 --> 00:45:34.380
believe in what
they're doing, even

00:45:34.380 --> 00:45:37.570
though everybody else
thinks they're wrong.

00:45:37.570 --> 00:45:41.160
For example, to get the violence
stopped in my own country,

00:45:41.160 --> 00:45:43.590
I got into direct dialogue
with organizations

00:45:43.590 --> 00:45:46.110
that were involved,
even though I totally

00:45:46.110 --> 00:45:48.490
condemned what they were doing.

00:45:48.490 --> 00:45:51.510
I asked them to state the
reasons for their violence,

00:45:51.510 --> 00:45:53.780
and they stated them.

00:45:53.780 --> 00:45:55.397
And I said-- well, two reasons.

00:45:55.397 --> 00:45:57.730
The British are in Ireland
defending their own interests

00:45:57.730 --> 00:45:58.410
by force.

00:45:58.410 --> 00:46:01.670
Therefore we have the right
to use force to put them out.

00:46:01.670 --> 00:46:03.830
And secondly, they're
preventing the Irish people

00:46:03.830 --> 00:46:06.740
from exercising their right
to self-determination.

00:46:06.740 --> 00:46:08.602
So I said, look,
reason number one

00:46:08.602 --> 00:46:10.310
used to be true in
the past, but it's not

00:46:10.310 --> 00:46:12.740
true in today's modern world.

00:46:12.740 --> 00:46:15.290
Britain has no economic
or strategic interest

00:46:15.290 --> 00:46:17.360
in being in Ireland today.

00:46:17.360 --> 00:46:19.100
Our problem is a
legacy of that past.

00:46:19.100 --> 00:46:21.150
We're a divided people.

00:46:21.150 --> 00:46:24.460
And secondly, the Irish
people, if you describe them

00:46:24.460 --> 00:46:26.460
as the people who live
on the island as a whole,

00:46:26.460 --> 00:46:28.620
have the right to
self-determination, yes.

00:46:28.620 --> 00:46:30.210
But unfortunately
they are divided as

00:46:30.210 --> 00:46:31.800
to how to exercise it.

00:46:31.800 --> 00:46:34.310
Therefore, it's
agreement we require.

00:46:34.310 --> 00:46:38.080
Their reply to me was, you
prove that and we'll chuck it.

00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:39.970
We'll stop the violence.

00:46:39.970 --> 00:46:42.910
So in my dialogue
with Gerry Adams,

00:46:42.910 --> 00:46:45.310
I was asking the British and
Irish governments to make

00:46:45.310 --> 00:46:48.280
a declaration which said that.

00:46:48.280 --> 00:46:53.690
And they did say it, the
Downing Street Declaration.

00:46:53.690 --> 00:46:56.090
In other words, even
though most people

00:46:56.090 --> 00:47:00.200
would disagree with the reasons,
then prove to these people

00:47:00.200 --> 00:47:03.950
that the reasons
didn't exist anymore.

00:47:03.950 --> 00:47:06.890
Now, I don't know, and I have
to admit that I don't fully

00:47:06.890 --> 00:47:11.662
understand the situation that
has led to these attacks.

00:47:11.662 --> 00:47:14.900
But an attempt should
be made to find out

00:47:14.900 --> 00:47:18.270
exactly why did they do it.

00:47:18.270 --> 00:47:21.740
And then address those
reasons, as well as--

00:47:21.740 --> 00:47:24.050
because no matter what
reason they did it for,

00:47:24.050 --> 00:47:27.110
their method of doing
it was appalling,

00:47:27.110 --> 00:47:31.940
and the people who died were
totally innocent people.

00:47:31.940 --> 00:47:34.760
And therefore they should
be brought to justice,

00:47:34.760 --> 00:47:37.230
and their organizations as well.

00:47:37.230 --> 00:47:40.190
But, as I say, it would
also be useful to know

00:47:40.190 --> 00:47:42.360
why did they do that.

00:47:42.360 --> 00:47:46.870
And why did an organized
group of people do that?

00:47:46.870 --> 00:47:47.877
What are the reasons?

00:47:47.877 --> 00:47:49.210
And address the reasons as well.

00:47:55.658 --> 00:47:56.650
AUDIENCE: Hi.

00:47:56.650 --> 00:47:59.700
Dr. Hume, I'm very
excited about the idea

00:47:59.700 --> 00:48:04.720
you were saying about the
referendum, how that kept

00:48:04.720 --> 00:48:07.090
people from co-opting the
process by showing that all

00:48:07.090 --> 00:48:08.900
the people were behind it.

00:48:08.900 --> 00:48:11.650
Now, the problem
is that last week I

00:48:11.650 --> 00:48:14.260
went and heard Paul Simon talk
about the Marshall Plan, which

00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:16.780
was behind the,
as you know, some

00:48:16.780 --> 00:48:20.020
of the foundations of the EU
and the peace that we've had

00:48:20.020 --> 00:48:22.120
in the last 40 years in Europe.

00:48:22.120 --> 00:48:24.190
And he said only
18% of Americans

00:48:24.190 --> 00:48:27.586
supported the Marshall Plan
when it was implemented.

00:48:27.586 --> 00:48:28.960
And he was
particularly concerned

00:48:28.960 --> 00:48:30.970
that right now
politicians in America

00:48:30.970 --> 00:48:36.640
couldn't go against the general
popular desire, which is not

00:48:36.640 --> 00:48:38.470
exactly towards
conflict resolution,

00:48:38.470 --> 00:48:40.910
at least not peaceful
conflict resolution.

00:48:40.910 --> 00:48:43.180
So I don't know
what my question is.

00:48:43.180 --> 00:48:46.390
I like your idea, and I'm
wondering how can you implement

00:48:46.390 --> 00:48:48.310
that idea in a general case?

00:48:48.310 --> 00:48:49.831
HUME: I don't understand you.

00:48:49.831 --> 00:48:52.720
[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

00:48:52.720 --> 00:48:55.665
Could you explain what
you're asking me about?

00:48:55.665 --> 00:48:57.040
AUDIENCE: The
question is, do you

00:48:57.040 --> 00:49:01.030
think it generalizes that you
can get a popular referendum

00:49:01.030 --> 00:49:02.656
to support a peaceful process?

00:49:02.656 --> 00:49:04.030
I guess that's
the short version.

00:49:04.030 --> 00:49:09.040
HUME: Well, when I was talking
about areas of conflict,

00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:10.764
I was talking about
divided communities

00:49:10.764 --> 00:49:12.430
in different parts
of the world that are

00:49:12.430 --> 00:49:14.350
conflicting with one another.

00:49:14.350 --> 00:49:17.680
Like the Middle East is a prime
example of it, for example.

00:49:17.680 --> 00:49:19.870
And again it's about territory.

00:49:19.870 --> 00:49:24.280
What I'm saying is, first
and foremost, end violence,

00:49:24.280 --> 00:49:26.770
because it has no role to
play in solving the problem.

00:49:26.770 --> 00:49:28.690
It only deepens the divisions.

00:49:28.690 --> 00:49:31.900
Secondly, get into
dialogue and talk

00:49:31.900 --> 00:49:36.160
and reach agreement as to how
you share pieces of earth.

00:49:36.160 --> 00:49:41.380
And then get the people to
approve of that in referenda.

00:49:41.380 --> 00:49:43.880
Then nobody can come out
with a gun and say, oh,

00:49:43.880 --> 00:49:45.570
we're sold don't.

00:49:45.570 --> 00:49:46.990
We have been sold out.

00:49:46.990 --> 00:49:51.760
They can't say that if the
people have voted for it.

00:49:51.760 --> 00:49:54.910
And that's why I think that
it's a very powerful element

00:49:54.910 --> 00:49:59.172
in a conflict
resolution situation

00:49:59.172 --> 00:50:00.130
and in a peace process.

00:50:04.620 --> 00:50:06.290
ZAVERI: Hi, my name
is Pedram Zaveri.

00:50:06.290 --> 00:50:08.390
I'm a graduate
student here at MIT

00:50:08.390 --> 00:50:10.250
and also a native
of Pakistan, which

00:50:10.250 --> 00:50:13.010
seems to be a lot in
the news these days.

00:50:13.010 --> 00:50:15.860
My question is that,
recently, polls in the US

00:50:15.860 --> 00:50:18.230
showed that 92% of
the US population

00:50:18.230 --> 00:50:22.220
is behind George Bush,
the political leadership,

00:50:22.220 --> 00:50:24.410
in the attacks
that have happened

00:50:24.410 --> 00:50:26.480
in the aftermath and
the military action

00:50:26.480 --> 00:50:27.650
against the Taliban.

00:50:27.650 --> 00:50:30.609
On the other side, 82%
of the Muslim population

00:50:30.609 --> 00:50:32.150
in many of the
countries have sort of

00:50:32.150 --> 00:50:35.300
thought of Osama bin
Laden, a terrorist,

00:50:35.300 --> 00:50:38.510
in some sense as a leader.

00:50:38.510 --> 00:50:40.160
Given those kind
of support coming

00:50:40.160 --> 00:50:42.360
from the people,
the populations,

00:50:42.360 --> 00:50:44.210
how do you see political
leadership, who

00:50:44.210 --> 00:50:47.370
thrive on such people,
masses, supporting them,

00:50:47.370 --> 00:50:49.880
how can they align
themselves into negotiation?

00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:53.530
It almost seems as though people
are happy with the war that's

00:50:53.530 --> 00:50:54.030
going on.

00:50:54.030 --> 00:50:55.655
They're happy that
there's retaliation,

00:50:55.655 --> 00:50:57.890
or they're happy that
a war is developing

00:50:57.890 --> 00:50:59.550
and somebody will win.

00:50:59.550 --> 00:51:02.120
So how do we move from
such winning the war

00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:05.990
and then winning the people over
to a conflict resolution which

00:51:05.990 --> 00:51:08.150
may not be totally
supported by people?

00:51:08.150 --> 00:51:12.390
HUME: Well, how you do
it is what I've said.

00:51:12.390 --> 00:51:16.790
First of all-- and I know that
this is what the people are

00:51:16.790 --> 00:51:18.230
supporting--

00:51:18.230 --> 00:51:20.570
working to bring to justice
the people who committed

00:51:20.570 --> 00:51:22.480
those terrible atrocities.

00:51:22.480 --> 00:51:24.350
A vast majority of the
people of the world

00:51:24.350 --> 00:51:28.000
support bringing those
people to justice.

00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:33.240
But what I'm talking about in
terms of conflict resolution

00:51:33.240 --> 00:51:36.990
where you have areas
of the world where

00:51:36.990 --> 00:51:39.890
two sections of people
are in conflict, who

00:51:39.890 --> 00:51:42.900
live in the same areas,
that their agreement should

00:51:42.900 --> 00:51:45.190
go to the people.

00:51:45.190 --> 00:51:48.880
Now, what we're talking about
here in the American situation

00:51:48.880 --> 00:51:56.250
in relation to those atrocities,
the facts haven't yet emerged.

00:51:56.250 --> 00:51:58.740
Therefore, people can't
make up their minds

00:51:58.740 --> 00:52:01.230
until the full facts do emerge.

00:52:01.230 --> 00:52:05.070
Like, first of all, who exactly
were the people who did this

00:52:05.070 --> 00:52:07.369
and why did they do it?

00:52:07.369 --> 00:52:09.910
And they certainly have to be
brought to justice for doing it

00:52:09.910 --> 00:52:13.300
because there's no justification
of any description for doing

00:52:13.300 --> 00:52:16.020
what they did, and they
should be brought to justice.

00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:21.520
But if the reasons gave
birth to people like that,

00:52:21.520 --> 00:52:25.420
and are likely to continue to
give birth to people like that,

00:52:25.420 --> 00:52:29.290
then the reasons should be
addressed as well in order

00:52:29.290 --> 00:52:33.090
to demonstrate to people on
the ground in those areas

00:52:33.090 --> 00:52:35.020
that those reasons don't exist.

00:52:35.020 --> 00:52:39.280
And if there is some bitterness
in those regions arising out

00:52:39.280 --> 00:52:42.630
of the past, as we know--

00:52:42.630 --> 00:52:46.790
I mean, our quarrel
started in 1689, you know.

00:52:46.790 --> 00:52:50.660
And therefore that
could still be there.

00:52:50.660 --> 00:52:52.630
While this country has
modernized and gone

00:52:52.630 --> 00:52:55.390
on and on and on,
many people would

00:52:55.390 --> 00:52:59.200
have forgotten completely
anything that happened

00:52:59.200 --> 00:53:01.210
even 20 or 30 years ago.

00:53:01.210 --> 00:53:04.690
So what are the reasons
there, is all I'm saying.

00:53:04.690 --> 00:53:06.500
I don't know what they are.

00:53:06.500 --> 00:53:10.860
I would like to know if there
were reasons and what they are.

00:53:10.860 --> 00:53:15.800
Or maybe they were just
traditional religious reasons

00:53:15.800 --> 00:53:19.300
from those type of people who
have a very strange notion

00:53:19.300 --> 00:53:20.504
about religion.

00:53:20.504 --> 00:53:22.420
I don't know what the
reasons were but I would

00:53:22.420 --> 00:53:23.544
like to know what they are.

00:53:23.544 --> 00:53:25.450
And then when they
are brought forward,

00:53:25.450 --> 00:53:28.690
they should be addressed.

00:53:28.690 --> 00:53:30.330
CLAY: Yes.

00:53:30.330 --> 00:53:32.650
AUDIENCE: Dr.
Hume, traditionally

00:53:32.650 --> 00:53:34.270
in Northern Ireland,
political power

00:53:34.270 --> 00:53:37.301
has grown from people who've
been successful as politicians,

00:53:37.301 --> 00:53:38.800
have been successful
because they've

00:53:38.800 --> 00:53:41.100
held their ground, because
they've stood firm,

00:53:41.100 --> 00:53:42.630
because they haven't changed.

00:53:42.630 --> 00:53:44.796
And I'm wondering whether,
in your case, whether you

00:53:44.796 --> 00:53:47.680
see the peace process as being
a vindication of a direction

00:53:47.680 --> 00:53:52.030
that you chose some time ago
on which you've held firm.

00:53:52.030 --> 00:53:54.970
Or have you changed
in your positions?

00:53:54.970 --> 00:53:59.800
And if you have changed, what
has that experience been like?

00:53:59.800 --> 00:54:02.810
HUME: Well, I
haven't changed much.

00:54:02.810 --> 00:54:05.330
I went into politics
to solve problems,

00:54:05.330 --> 00:54:07.552
to solve a particular problem.

00:54:07.552 --> 00:54:12.210
And in my first
election in 1969,

00:54:12.210 --> 00:54:15.580
in my election literature,
which can be read,

00:54:15.580 --> 00:54:18.700
I said I was seeking
a mandate to find

00:54:18.700 --> 00:54:23.440
a social democratic party,
and I wanted to get away

00:54:23.440 --> 00:54:26.890
from the flag-waving politics.

00:54:26.890 --> 00:54:32.210
And that the unity
of our country,

00:54:32.210 --> 00:54:33.820
which we would
support, could only

00:54:33.820 --> 00:54:35.636
come about with the
consent of the majority

00:54:35.636 --> 00:54:36.760
of the people in the north.

00:54:36.760 --> 00:54:39.510
In other words, it could
only come about by agreement.

00:54:39.510 --> 00:54:43.210
Now, we were saying
that in 1969.

00:54:43.210 --> 00:54:48.860
At last, 32 years later, the
whole of nationalist Ireland

00:54:48.860 --> 00:54:52.430
are now saying the same thing,
but it took a bit of time.

00:54:52.430 --> 00:54:56.330
But, also, our
approach to the problem

00:54:56.330 --> 00:54:58.910
hasn't changed throughout
our existence as a party.

00:54:58.910 --> 00:55:00.840
Because the problem
hadn't changed,

00:55:00.840 --> 00:55:04.114
therefore neither did our
approach to solving it.

00:55:04.114 --> 00:55:05.780
And our approach to
solving it was based

00:55:05.780 --> 00:55:07.550
on our analysis of the problem.

00:55:07.550 --> 00:55:10.790
Number one, we're
a divided people,

00:55:10.790 --> 00:55:12.290
not a divided piece of earth.

00:55:12.290 --> 00:55:16.940
Therefore, we're totally and
absolutely opposed to violence.

00:55:16.940 --> 00:55:20.060
Secondly, we're divided on
three sets of relationships,

00:55:20.060 --> 00:55:21.660
as I said earlier.

00:55:21.660 --> 00:55:24.230
And those should be the
agenda at any talks,

00:55:24.230 --> 00:55:26.840
and the two governments
should be working together

00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:29.330
to reach agreement
with all the parties.

00:55:29.330 --> 00:55:31.100
And thirdly, when
agreement is reached,

00:55:31.100 --> 00:55:35.390
it should be approved by the
people and not the politicians.

00:55:35.390 --> 00:55:36.440
That was our policy.

00:55:36.440 --> 00:55:39.290
It's all on the record
down the 30 years.

00:55:39.290 --> 00:55:42.290
We stuck by it and
stuck by it, as I said.

00:55:42.290 --> 00:55:44.660
And I kept using the same
language all the time.

00:55:44.660 --> 00:55:46.850
They call it Hume-speak
now, you know.

00:55:46.850 --> 00:55:50.080
Because I kept saying
the same things.

00:55:50.080 --> 00:55:52.430
It's the old pitcher
in me, you know.

00:55:52.430 --> 00:55:54.890
When you're out to
persuade people,

00:55:54.890 --> 00:55:57.560
you don't persuade them in
one sentence or one speech.

00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:59.420
You have to keep at it.

00:55:59.420 --> 00:56:01.760
Now, when a man in a pub
uses the language back to me,

00:56:01.760 --> 00:56:06.340
I realize, right, I can move
on now and change my language.

00:56:06.340 --> 00:56:11.840
But, as I was saying,
we have stood by that.

00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:15.040
And the people are aware
that we have done that.

00:56:15.040 --> 00:56:20.640
And, as I say, what certain
unionists haven't realized

00:56:20.640 --> 00:56:23.530
is that the whole of what's
called nationalist Ireland now

00:56:23.530 --> 00:56:26.810
accepts that the
unity of the country

00:56:26.810 --> 00:56:29.030
can only come about with
the consent of the majority

00:56:29.030 --> 00:56:31.155
of the people of the north,
as well as the majority

00:56:31.155 --> 00:56:32.630
of the people of the south.

00:56:32.630 --> 00:56:35.750
Divided people, therefore
agreement of sides.

00:56:35.750 --> 00:56:38.000
And that's been our consistent
position throughout,

00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:40.280
and the people know that.

00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:43.430
And, of course,
certain other parties

00:56:43.430 --> 00:56:46.550
who felt that the way to
solve the Irish problem

00:56:46.550 --> 00:56:51.450
was through violence,
they recognized clearly

00:56:51.450 --> 00:56:55.880
that that was completely
wrong, and that the strategy

00:56:55.880 --> 00:56:59.120
and tactics of that was
also completely wrong.

00:56:59.120 --> 00:57:01.760
And, of course, you
can't be looking

00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:04.520
to defend the human
rights of your people

00:57:04.520 --> 00:57:07.040
if your method undermines the
most fundamental human right

00:57:07.040 --> 00:57:10.460
of all, the right to life.

00:57:10.460 --> 00:57:13.730
And therefore, as I say,
I have every confidence

00:57:13.730 --> 00:57:17.510
that the people in Ireland
know exactly not only what

00:57:17.510 --> 00:57:21.050
we have done to represent them
but that we have stood firm

00:57:21.050 --> 00:57:25.126
on our policies and convictions.

00:57:25.126 --> 00:57:26.750
CLAY: We have four
people here and they

00:57:26.750 --> 00:57:28.340
will be our last questioners.

00:57:28.340 --> 00:57:30.084
The first person.

00:57:30.084 --> 00:57:30.750
AUDIENCE: Hello.

00:57:30.750 --> 00:57:33.270
Thank you for
speaking this evening.

00:57:33.270 --> 00:57:35.100
Earlier in your
speech, you mentioned

00:57:35.100 --> 00:57:39.120
that you were very successful
in bringing economic interests

00:57:39.120 --> 00:57:42.810
into Ireland, or
gained the promises

00:57:42.810 --> 00:57:45.360
for that following
a peace process,

00:57:45.360 --> 00:57:48.330
in particular the
International Fund for Ireland.

00:57:48.330 --> 00:57:51.180
And you mentioned
briefly that you

00:57:51.180 --> 00:57:55.620
had both the very strong
educational background

00:57:55.620 --> 00:57:59.220
of your people, and you had
the close ties with America.

00:57:59.220 --> 00:58:02.800
And, looking to
generalize that success,

00:58:02.800 --> 00:58:05.790
how do you think
other countries where

00:58:05.790 --> 00:58:08.910
there are economic
problems that are leading

00:58:08.910 --> 00:58:15.330
to the lack of peace, how
can they learn from it

00:58:15.330 --> 00:58:20.520
and form some more basis
for a peace process?

00:58:20.520 --> 00:58:22.500
HUME: Well, of course,
if they address

00:58:22.500 --> 00:58:27.260
the center of their conflict
and they reach agreement,

00:58:27.260 --> 00:58:29.010
they then create
the circumstances

00:58:29.010 --> 00:58:31.810
where they're working together.

00:58:31.810 --> 00:58:35.440
And in many areas of course--

00:58:35.440 --> 00:58:37.650
and I was talking about
this earlier today.

00:58:37.650 --> 00:58:43.920
In many areas of the world
where there's terrible poverty,

00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:47.760
there's also a major
lack of education.

00:58:47.760 --> 00:58:51.240
And, as I have said,
when we're sending aid

00:58:51.240 --> 00:58:54.060
to third-world
countries, we should also

00:58:54.060 --> 00:58:58.239
be making sure that they
get an educational system.

00:58:58.239 --> 00:59:00.780
Because the aid can be used in
a week, and then the next week

00:59:00.780 --> 00:59:02.820
they're looking for more.

00:59:02.820 --> 00:59:06.240
Whereas the real
wealth is its people,

00:59:06.240 --> 00:59:08.760
and it's people who create.

00:59:08.760 --> 00:59:10.950
And people are far
more equipped to create

00:59:10.950 --> 00:59:12.640
when they're educated.

00:59:12.640 --> 00:59:16.410
And education-- and this is my
own experience that tells me

00:59:16.410 --> 00:59:17.100
this--

00:59:17.100 --> 00:59:20.580
is the major factor in
the economic development

00:59:20.580 --> 00:59:22.140
of any country.

00:59:22.140 --> 00:59:24.900
And therefore it should be
a major factor, particularly

00:59:24.900 --> 00:59:27.030
in the third world and
in poorer countries,

00:59:27.030 --> 00:59:29.940
getting education
in there to develop.

00:59:29.940 --> 00:59:32.880
I mean, in my own
part of the world,

00:59:32.880 --> 00:59:35.475
I can see how education
transformed our society.

00:59:38.420 --> 00:59:43.650
I was the first generation,
people of my age,

00:59:43.650 --> 00:59:46.620
to get educated in
Northern Ireland who

00:59:46.620 --> 00:59:49.090
didn't come from a rich family.

00:59:49.090 --> 00:59:51.420
My father was
unemployed and I was

00:59:51.420 --> 00:59:53.340
the eldest of seven
children, yet I went right

00:59:53.340 --> 00:59:54.810
through to university.

00:59:54.810 --> 00:59:58.590
Because the very first
year of the new system,

00:59:58.590 --> 01:00:02.640
the 11-Plus exam, as it was
called, I got the scholarship.

01:00:02.640 --> 01:00:04.500
Before that, there
was no education

01:00:04.500 --> 01:00:08.490
available at high school
level or university level

01:00:08.490 --> 01:00:11.730
to people whose parents
couldn't afford to pay for it.

01:00:11.730 --> 01:00:14.860
That transformed our society.

01:00:14.860 --> 01:00:18.030
And if you look at Ireland
today, for the first time

01:00:18.030 --> 01:00:20.880
ever the Irish economy
is self-sufficient.

01:00:20.880 --> 01:00:21.570
Why?

01:00:21.570 --> 01:00:24.270
Because we now have a
total educational system

01:00:24.270 --> 01:00:26.050
throughout the whole island.

01:00:26.050 --> 01:00:29.010
In other words, once again
coming back to my principle,

01:00:29.010 --> 01:00:31.440
respect for humanity.

01:00:31.440 --> 01:00:35.100
Human beings are the only
wealth we have in the world.

01:00:35.100 --> 01:00:39.630
Make sure that they're,
most are able to create that

01:00:39.630 --> 01:00:42.780
by making sure that they're
as fully developed as possible

01:00:42.780 --> 01:00:44.460
with their own
skills and talents

01:00:44.460 --> 01:00:46.900
through an educational system.

01:00:46.900 --> 01:00:48.890
And, indeed, there's nowhere--

01:00:48.890 --> 01:00:51.870
and I'm talking there
about normal education,

01:00:51.870 --> 01:00:54.370
like going to primary school,
and going to secondary school,

01:00:54.370 --> 01:00:56.640
and going to university.

01:00:56.640 --> 01:01:00.060
And yet I'm saying
that in a building

01:01:00.060 --> 01:01:04.640
where the modernization
of education is fantastic.

01:01:04.640 --> 01:01:05.790
And what you're doing--

01:01:05.790 --> 01:01:08.980
and I'm talking about
the Institute here--

01:01:08.980 --> 01:01:12.330
not only to develop
the skills and talents

01:01:12.330 --> 01:01:16.810
in a high-tech world,
but also to create out

01:01:16.810 --> 01:01:22.960
there the employment in
this whole new field.

01:01:22.960 --> 01:01:27.010
I mean, it's just proving how
societies can be transformed

01:01:27.010 --> 01:01:29.150
and what a difference
it can make.

01:01:29.150 --> 01:01:33.560
And it's education that's
the first step on the road.

01:01:33.560 --> 01:01:35.825
AUDIENCE: Dr. Hume,
it's a great opportunity

01:01:35.825 --> 01:01:38.480
to meet somebody like you.

01:01:38.480 --> 01:01:41.660
For somebody like me who was
born and have been living

01:01:41.660 --> 01:01:43.940
in an area of
conflict for 30 years,

01:01:43.940 --> 01:01:46.130
being a Middle Eastern
myself, a Jordanian

01:01:46.130 --> 01:01:50.030
from a Palestinian
origin, I really--

01:01:50.030 --> 01:01:52.220
we have been all
as Middle Eastern,

01:01:52.220 --> 01:01:58.460
I think-- looking at the Irish
experience with great interest.

01:01:58.460 --> 01:02:02.860
And having listened
to your principles,

01:02:02.860 --> 01:02:05.210
do you think that
resolving conflict

01:02:05.210 --> 01:02:11.030
in a situation like Ireland
could be somehow copied

01:02:11.030 --> 01:02:15.890
in a case where conflict is
under a situation of occupation

01:02:15.890 --> 01:02:18.890
rather than just
division of people?

01:02:18.890 --> 01:02:19.400
HUME: Well.

01:02:19.400 --> 01:02:20.233
AUDIENCE: Thank you.

01:02:20.233 --> 01:02:24.920
HUME: You see, in Ireland
one of the political views

01:02:24.920 --> 01:02:31.550
was that a part of the island
was being occupied by Britain.

01:02:31.550 --> 01:02:34.880
But what I'm saying
is the principles

01:02:34.880 --> 01:02:38.210
at the heart of our agreement
are the exact same principles

01:02:38.210 --> 01:02:42.780
that ended conflict between
the peoples of Europe.

01:02:42.780 --> 01:02:44.950
We had two world wars.

01:02:44.950 --> 01:02:48.130
And when you apply those
principles to the Middle East,

01:02:48.130 --> 01:02:50.680
the first message
to get over to them

01:02:50.680 --> 01:02:55.150
is that they have
a quarrel, yes.

01:02:55.150 --> 01:02:57.580
But the first thing to
learn is that violence

01:02:57.580 --> 01:03:01.460
in no shape or form will
solve their quarrel.

01:03:01.460 --> 01:03:05.090
It will only make it worse
because people on both sides

01:03:05.090 --> 01:03:06.772
will lose their lives.

01:03:06.772 --> 01:03:08.480
Therefore, the first
thing they should do

01:03:08.480 --> 01:03:11.460
is stop their violence.

01:03:11.460 --> 01:03:12.960
And that's common sense.

01:03:12.960 --> 01:03:14.460
The second thing
they should then do

01:03:14.460 --> 01:03:20.385
is sit down, and talk,
and discuss how they share

01:03:20.385 --> 01:03:21.825
the piece of earth together.

01:03:24.047 --> 01:03:25.630
Well, you're talking
about occupation,

01:03:25.630 --> 01:03:28.570
but how they actually share
the piece of earth together.

01:03:28.570 --> 01:03:34.230
And they do it in a manner where
it's people that have rights,

01:03:34.230 --> 01:03:36.576
and not territory.

01:03:36.576 --> 01:03:37.950
And that's what
I'm talking about

01:03:37.950 --> 01:03:40.770
in terms of our agreement,
that the government,

01:03:40.770 --> 01:03:43.110
the new government of
Northern Ireland, all sections

01:03:43.110 --> 01:03:46.880
of our people, are
in the government

01:03:46.880 --> 01:03:49.631
of that piece of earth.

01:03:49.631 --> 01:03:51.630
It's people that are
running the piece of earth,

01:03:51.630 --> 01:03:54.800
not the piece of earth
running the people.

01:03:54.800 --> 01:03:58.850
And the same principle could
apply to the Middle East,

01:03:58.850 --> 01:04:02.030
I think, if they just
sit and reach agreement.

01:04:02.030 --> 01:04:05.070
Because, once again,
let's not forget

01:04:05.070 --> 01:04:07.960
that people were born
in a particular place.

01:04:07.960 --> 01:04:10.122
They didn't choose
to be born there.

01:04:10.122 --> 01:04:12.330
Other people say, you
shouldn't have been born there.

01:04:12.330 --> 01:04:14.220
It should have been me.

01:04:14.220 --> 01:04:18.430
But, as I say, that
being the case,

01:04:18.430 --> 01:04:23.540
they should agree how they
share a piece of earth,

01:04:23.540 --> 01:04:26.390
not the piece of
earth governs them.

01:04:26.390 --> 01:04:28.940
Because, as I said
before, what is a piece

01:04:28.940 --> 01:04:31.514
of earth if there's no people?

01:04:31.514 --> 01:04:33.430
So they shouldn't be
fighting about territory.

01:04:33.430 --> 01:04:37.810
They should be agreeing as
to how they live together

01:04:37.810 --> 01:04:40.040
in territory.

01:04:40.040 --> 01:04:43.222
And, also, of course
I've often said--

01:04:43.222 --> 01:04:45.680
and it's been misinterpreted
deliberately by some of my own

01:04:45.680 --> 01:04:47.420
political opponents--

01:04:47.420 --> 01:04:51.097
we're living in a
post-nationalist world today.

01:04:51.097 --> 01:04:53.180
There are those who think
that the nation-state is

01:04:53.180 --> 01:04:55.550
an eternal concept.

01:04:55.550 --> 01:04:57.080
But before the
nation states, there

01:04:57.080 --> 01:05:00.540
were city states, et
cetera, et cetera.

01:05:00.540 --> 01:05:04.940
And as the world got smaller,
the nation states grew.

01:05:04.940 --> 01:05:09.280
Now, as the world is
getting smaller still,

01:05:09.280 --> 01:05:12.440
countries are coming
closer together.

01:05:12.440 --> 01:05:15.280
Like in Europe
today, we don't have

01:05:15.280 --> 01:05:17.590
independent European countries.

01:05:17.590 --> 01:05:20.680
We have interdependent
European countries,

01:05:20.680 --> 01:05:22.180
because they're all
working together

01:05:22.180 --> 01:05:23.830
in their common interests.

01:05:23.830 --> 01:05:26.440
And you take the most
fundamental industry of all--

01:05:26.440 --> 01:05:29.010
the industries that
provide your food--

01:05:29.010 --> 01:05:32.830
all decisions in agriculture
for 15 of the countries

01:05:32.830 --> 01:05:36.610
are taken at European level,
not at national level.

01:05:36.610 --> 01:05:40.390
So the world evolves,
and the nation-state

01:05:40.390 --> 01:05:41.770
is not an eternal concept.

01:05:41.770 --> 01:05:43.000
We've moved beyond it.

01:05:43.000 --> 01:05:46.300
But what doesn't change
is that it's people

01:05:46.300 --> 01:05:48.480
who are living in the world.

01:05:48.480 --> 01:05:50.977
And it's people who
have to live together.

01:05:50.977 --> 01:05:52.560
Therefore it's people
who should agree

01:05:52.560 --> 01:05:55.020
on how they live
together, not deciding

01:05:55.020 --> 01:05:57.930
that one piece of earth
has to get some people out

01:05:57.930 --> 01:06:00.830
of it and other people into it.

01:06:00.830 --> 01:06:02.810
CLAY: Yes, sir.

01:06:02.810 --> 01:06:04.160
AUDIENCE: Hi.

01:06:04.160 --> 01:06:07.970
I'm concerned that this
country's current reaction

01:06:07.970 --> 01:06:14.930
to the tragedies of
September 11 will simply

01:06:14.930 --> 01:06:20.510
be part of a cycle of
violence that we've

01:06:20.510 --> 01:06:21.950
only just begun to see.

01:06:21.950 --> 01:06:26.750
And I'm concerned
that, in reacting

01:06:26.750 --> 01:06:32.720
to the events of September
11, we're not seeking justice,

01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:37.280
and rather we're seeking
vengeance with violence.

01:06:37.280 --> 01:06:38.960
Part of that concern
is due to the fact

01:06:38.960 --> 01:06:42.650
that we haven't
paid any attention

01:06:42.650 --> 01:06:46.070
to seeking the role
of the United Nations

01:06:46.070 --> 01:06:48.140
in seeking justice.

01:06:48.140 --> 01:06:51.380
And I was wondering if you could
comment on any potential roles

01:06:51.380 --> 01:06:53.600
that the United
Nations could play,

01:06:53.600 --> 01:06:57.110
and how we can
strengthen that role

01:06:57.110 --> 01:07:01.702
and get the United States
to subscribe to it.

01:07:01.702 --> 01:07:03.410
HUME: Well, I've
already spelled out what

01:07:03.410 --> 01:07:04.682
I think about that situation.

01:07:04.682 --> 01:07:06.140
And as I said, the
people should be

01:07:06.140 --> 01:07:08.630
brought to justice, and that
it should be done so in a way

01:07:08.630 --> 01:07:10.430
that innocent
people don't suffer.

01:07:10.430 --> 01:07:12.620
And it should also
address the reasons.

01:07:12.620 --> 01:07:15.610
And another way, of course--
you made a good point there--

01:07:15.610 --> 01:07:18.380
that the reasons could
be brought forward fully

01:07:18.380 --> 01:07:20.360
and clearly and
objectively would

01:07:20.360 --> 01:07:22.820
be if the United Nations
were to go into that area

01:07:22.820 --> 01:07:27.800
and find out what was the
reasoning behind all of this,

01:07:27.800 --> 01:07:31.550
and explain that and
make their proposals as

01:07:31.550 --> 01:07:37.575
to how to ensure that that
sort of thing is not repeated.

01:07:37.575 --> 01:07:38.509
CLAY: Last question.

01:07:41.494 --> 01:07:42.910
AUDIENCE: Dr. Hume,
thank you very

01:07:42.910 --> 01:07:47.260
much for coming to speak about
issues of conflict resolution

01:07:47.260 --> 01:07:49.224
to the academic community
of the Boston area.

01:07:49.224 --> 01:07:50.890
I'm a graduate student
from the Fletcher

01:07:50.890 --> 01:07:55.210
School of Law and Diplomacy
just down the road.

01:07:55.210 --> 01:07:58.240
You mentioned actors who
attempt to undermine resolution

01:07:58.240 --> 01:08:00.850
efforts, and you mentioned
that the people should come out

01:08:00.850 --> 01:08:05.170
against such
unrepresentative factions.

01:08:05.170 --> 01:08:07.780
But my question is, how do
your principles of conflict

01:08:07.780 --> 01:08:12.580
resolution relate to a complex
conflict such as the one

01:08:12.580 --> 01:08:15.310
in the Democratic
Republic of Congo,

01:08:15.310 --> 01:08:18.189
in which those who have a
vested interest in fueling

01:08:18.189 --> 01:08:22.210
a conflict such as a proxy
war for natural resources

01:08:22.210 --> 01:08:26.200
are far more powerful and
empowered than those who suffer

01:08:26.200 --> 01:08:27.729
from the conflict,
even those who

01:08:27.729 --> 01:08:31.000
suffer on both sides of a
conflict that benefits others?

01:08:33.660 --> 01:08:36.271
HUME: Well, in areas of
that nature of course,

01:08:36.271 --> 01:08:37.979
where you have what
you're talking about,

01:08:37.979 --> 01:08:40.830
forms of dictatorship,
et cetera,

01:08:40.830 --> 01:08:44.850
that's what the United
Nations are in existence for,

01:08:44.850 --> 01:08:47.069
to deal with problems
of that nature.

01:08:47.069 --> 01:08:48.899
And the United Nations
should positively

01:08:48.899 --> 01:08:53.321
move into areas like that
and describe to the world--

01:08:53.321 --> 01:08:54.779
first of all,
describe to the world

01:08:54.779 --> 01:08:57.120
the situation that
exists in order

01:08:57.120 --> 01:09:00.720
to put pressure on those
who are abusing power,

01:09:00.720 --> 01:09:03.180
and create the
process which will

01:09:03.180 --> 01:09:07.770
lead to a just
society in such areas.

01:09:07.770 --> 01:09:12.840
But, you know, in dealing
with an issue like that,

01:09:12.840 --> 01:09:16.020
I would like to study the
whole problem in depth

01:09:16.020 --> 01:09:19.080
before, and then come up with
proposals to deal with it.

01:09:19.080 --> 01:09:22.140
I was talking in general
terms about areas of conflict

01:09:22.140 --> 01:09:26.010
where the conflict is clear
between two communities.

01:09:26.010 --> 01:09:27.990
But other areas of
more complicated

01:09:27.990 --> 01:09:30.300
stuff that United Nations--

01:09:30.300 --> 01:09:33.479
and of course, as I've often
said about the United Nations,

01:09:33.479 --> 01:09:36.660
they shouldn't just be sending
armies into areas of conflict.

01:09:36.660 --> 01:09:38.250
They should be sending
in a philosophy

01:09:38.250 --> 01:09:41.120
as well to solve the problem.

01:09:41.120 --> 01:09:44.210
Because normally what happens
in divided societies when

01:09:44.210 --> 01:09:46.990
you send an army
onto the streets,

01:09:46.990 --> 01:09:50.490
it may stop the violence
but what happens?

01:09:50.490 --> 01:09:52.890
In each side they keep getting
more and more guns waiting

01:09:52.890 --> 01:09:56.040
for the army to leave.

01:09:56.040 --> 01:09:59.110
And therefore they should
be taking in the philosophy.

01:09:59.110 --> 01:10:02.210
And I've also been proposing
recently at European level,

01:10:02.210 --> 01:10:04.470
at the European
Union, given that it's

01:10:04.470 --> 01:10:07.080
the best example in the history
of the world of conflict

01:10:07.080 --> 01:10:08.400
resolution.

01:10:08.400 --> 01:10:10.860
While it has many departments,
normal departments

01:10:10.860 --> 01:10:13.560
of agriculture, et cetera,
and economic departments,

01:10:13.560 --> 01:10:17.510
it should also have a department
of peace and reconciliation.

01:10:17.510 --> 01:10:19.400
And there should be a
European commissioner

01:10:19.400 --> 01:10:22.150
for peace and reconciliation.

01:10:22.150 --> 01:10:25.130
And they should take
the philosophy down

01:10:25.130 --> 01:10:28.180
into the areas of
conflict and talk

01:10:28.180 --> 01:10:30.760
to the different sides
involved, and bring

01:10:30.760 --> 01:10:32.664
in the philosophy, not an army.

01:10:35.620 --> 01:10:36.590
CLAY: Okay.

01:10:36.590 --> 01:10:37.880
Thank you very. much.

01:10:37.880 --> 01:10:41.230
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDS]

